# Repo-root .gitignore (companion to app/.gitignore, which handles the SPA subtree).
#
# Per gitignore semantics, leading-slash patterns (e.g. `/supabase/functions`)
# are anchored to THIS FILE'S directory (the repo root); without a leading
# slash, patterns would match at any depth and would accidentally shadow
# tracked app/supabase/{functions,migrations,seed.sql} and app/tests/
# subtree content. So we deliberately use leading slashes for every rule
# below -- each pattern here is repo-root-only by construction. This
# separation lets the SPA subtree carry its own .gitignore conventions
# in app/.gitignore without coordination between the two ignore files.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-host operational symlinks -- RECREATED PER SESSION, NOT IN TRACKED GIT
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `app/docs/ops-notes.md` H3 §'Empirical-closure prerequisites #2' documents
# the protocol that creates these at capture time:
#   ln -s $L/app/supabase/migrations $L/supabase/migrations
#   ln -s $L/app/supabase/functions  $L/supabase/functions
#   ln -s $L/app/supabase/seed.sql   $L/supabase/seed.sql
# They are intentionally OUT-OF-TREE symlinks: the real source of truth lives
# under `app/supabase/`. These exist only because the Supabase CLI resolves
# `supabase/migrations`, `supabase/functions`, `supabase/seed.sql` relative
# to the project root (per `[db.seed] sql_paths` in supabase/config.toml +
# the CLI's hardcoded paths/internal-load.py for functions). Without these
# symlinks, `supabase db reset` applies zero migrations AND `public.cameras`
# would NOT exist, breaking the bug-e regression spec's service-role INSERT
# into `public.cameras` BEFORE the BRAND `?? FALLBACK` TypeError can fire
# (see ops-notes §Bug E lock-in workflow).
/supabase/functions
/supabase/migrations
/supabase/seed.sql

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-host stale duplicate of the bug-e baseline regeneration output
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `app/tests/e2e/_baseline-run.json` is the TRACKED canonical baseline
# (committed at 90c41ee test(e2e): OVERWRITE baseline sequence with REAL
# Playwright timings, regenerated by capture-v6.sh Phase M ops-ci auto-commit
# via `scrub_and_build.py`). The root-level `tests/` directory in this repo
# contains a single stray file (`tests/e2e/_baseline-run.json`) that was
# copied there by an earlier basher's path assumption (basher `cd app && ls
# tests/...` resolved under `app/` not under repo root). It is NOT tracking
# anything real -- the always-fresh on-disk version lives at
# `app/tests/e2e/_baseline-run.json` which is committed. Track the canonical
# location only.
/tests/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future per-host operational entries go below, each with a comment naming
# the ops-notes section that justifies gitignoring it. Do NOT add patterns
# WITHOUT a comment, so the next maintainer can understand why the rule
# exists without spelunking through `git log --grep=ops-notes`.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
